From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jun Matsushita <jun@mercury.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:40:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] buck2: let `buck2 kill` wait for the BES server to
 acknowledge the daemon's events

`buck2 kill --bes-drain-timeout <duration>` asks the daemon to deliver what
its event sink still holds. It then waits, up to the timeout, until the
server has acknowledged it, and only then exits. The result names any
invocation still unacknowledged.

`buck2 debug flush-bes` does the same for finished commands without stopping
the daemon.

Without the flag a kill behaves as before. A CI runner can use it so a job's
last build reaches the server before the runner goes away.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
